abstract: 'The Bute Inlet Ocean Observing Station (BIOOS) provides high-resolution
  profiling in Bute Inlet, a fjord on the British Columbia coast. A C-PROOF (Canadian
  Pacific Robotic Ocean Observing Facility) Wirewalker, a wave-powered profiler, is
  moored in the central fjord, measuring conductivity, temperature, pressure, and
  dissolved oxygen through the water column. Two versions of the record are included:
  provisional data offloaded directly from the instrument, which is the more complete,
  and real-time data received via satellite, which is the more current.'
